- `expand/tools/competency_map.py` - the map, categories and A/B source
  attribution from the same command's Steps 3-5, as code
- `expand/tools/github_source.py` - from the same command's Step 1e (GitHub
  profile plus every public repo, not only pinned ones), through the public
  REST API and the jobseek fetch/guard stack
- `expand/tools/web_source.py` - from the same command's Step 1f (other URLs
  in the profile), narrowed to quoted pointers with a standing review note
- `tailor/tailor.md` and `tailor/README.md` also incorporate guidance text
  from ai-job-search .claude/skills/job-application-assistant/
  03-writing-style.md, 05-cv-templates.md and 08-application-forms.md
- `tailor/tools/latex_templates/resume.tex.tmpl` - reimplemented from
  ai-job-search's moderncv CV template (no local copy of the upstream file
  was available to vendor verbatim in this environment; structure and intent
  - moderncv `classic` style, name/address/contact header, section-per-block
  layout - follow the upstream template)
- `tailor/tools/latex_templates/cover.cls` - reimplemented from
  ai-job-search's `cover.cls` why-me/cover-letter class, same reason as above
- `tailor/tools/render_latex.py` - new renderer (Markdown -> the templates
  above) written for jobseek's own resume Markdown shape, replacing
  ai-job-search's own LaTeX-authoring convention
- `tailor/tools/compile_latex.py`, `tailor/tools/verify_pdf.py`,
  `tailor/tools/verify_layout.py` - reimplemented from ai-job-search's
  compile-and-inspect loop and its `verify_pdf.py`/`verify_layout.py`
  (page count, ATS text-layer presence, layout overflow/holes), adapted to
  jobseek's export-tool exit-code conventions (0/1/2, matching
  `export_resume.py`)
- `tailor/tools/latex_pipeline.py` - new orchestrator tying the four files
  above into the render/compile/verify/re-render loop; not present as a
  single file upstream
- `tools/notion_sync.py`, `tools/notion_client.py`,
  `.claude/commands/notion-sync.md` - reimplemented from ai-job-search's
  `/notion-sync` command (one-way sync of the tracker/shortlist into a
  Notion database), rebased on jobseek's state/seen_jobs.json schema and
  Director/VP rank fields, and on OAuth-based Notion MCP access (no stored
  Notion API token) instead of ai-job-search's own auth approach
- `dashboard/build.py` - from `.claude/commands/html-report.md` (status buckets,
  stats rules, inline-SVG charts, filterable table, escaping rule), rebased on
  jobseek's tracker/seen_jobs/last_run; adds ranked-posting rows, flags,
  sources and follow-up due dates, and drops the outcome.md merge
- `tools/upskill_state.py` - from `.claude/skills/upskill/SKILL.md` Steps 2-3
  (the deterministic aggregate-mode merge: tracker/ranked dedupe on
  company+title, fit/rank-score weights, blank-fit_rating and missing-gaps
  skip rules), rebased on the jobseek layout and rank_state.norm
- `upskill/upskill.md` - from `.claude/skills/upskill/SKILL.md` (skill-gap
  heatmap, learning plan, study order, report format and trust rules),
  specialized for a Director/VP AI-strategy search (leadership/strategy
  competencies, not only technical skills) and rebased on jobseek's
  state-through-tools rule

The portal CLIs in ai-job-search derive from Mikkel Krogholm's skills repo
(acknowledged in its README); none of them are copied here.

## Copied verbatim, whole directory

- `linkedin/app/` - copied in full from ai-job-search's `linkedin_mcp/`
  (an Electron app holding a signed-in LinkedIn session and a cross-platform
  stdio/local-endpoint MCP relay: `src/main.js`, `src/server.js`,
  `src/extractors.js`, `src/pacing.js`, `src/cache.js`, `src/paths.js`,
  `src/urls.js`, `src/format.js`, `src/tools.js`, `bin/linkedin-mcp.js`,
  `package.json`, and its own `tests/` and fixture HTML) - unchanged in
  behavior, tests, Windows/macOS support, and pacing/rate-limit caps; only
  its location moved, from a standalone repo's `linkedin_mcp/` to
  `linkedin/app/` inside this one

## Adapted, new for the jobseek integration

- `linkedin/client.py` - new: a Python client that speaks the same
  newline-delimited JSON-RPC wire format as `linkedin/app/src/server.js`
  directly (mirrors `linkedin/app/src/paths.js`'s endpoint resolution), so
  jobseek's tools and MCP server never have to spawn Node at call time
- `linkedin/source.py` - new: the run-alerts LinkedIn source, mapping
  `linkedin/app`'s `linkedin_search_jobs` results into the exact candidate
  shape `tools/alert_state.py` already consumes (same job_key dedupe,
  same seen_jobs.json, no parallel pipeline)
- `mcp/tools.py`'s `linkedin_search`, `get_job`, `search_people` - new:
  jobseek MCP passthroughs to `linkedin/client.py`
- `.claude/commands/run-alerts.md` - extended (not rewritten) to run
  `linkedin/source.py candidates` alongside the Gmail alert ingest

